  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $X$ be a finite set of size $n$ and $H(n)$ be such that there is a function $f:\\{A : A\\subseteq X\\}\\to X$ so that for every $Y\\subseteq X$ with $\\lvert Y\\rvert \\geq H(n)$ we have $ \\{ f(A) : A\\subseteq Y\\}=X. $ Prove that $ H(n)-\\log_2 n \\to \\infty. $ ",
